Save the web page's Model settings through a symlinked run config.

In the container /opt/strata/strata-<tag>.json is a link into
$STRATA_DATA/config/ (docker-entrypoint.sh, #1244). runconfig.save()
os.replace()s the link itself, so a change from the About tab lands in the
container's own filesystem and is gone on the next start, while the file on
the volume keeps the old values. Resolving the path first writes the file the
link points to, and keeps the .bak beside it.

Retire when upstream's runconfig.save() resolves the path (or the entrypoint
stops linking the config).

diff --git a/serve/runconfig.py b/serve/runconfig.py
index 472b002..065cb12 100644
--- a/serve/runconfig.py
+++ b/serve/runconfig.py
@@ -163,7 +163,7 @@ def apply(cfg: dict, changes: dict) -> tuple[dict, list[str]]:
 
 def save(path: str | Path, cfg: dict) -> Path:
     """The config written whole (a temporary file moved over the old one), the earlier one kept as <name>.bak."""
-    path = Path(path)
+    path = Path(path).resolve()                       # a link (the container's): write the file it points to
     bak = path.with_name(path.name + ".bak")
     shutil.copyfile(path, bak)
     tmp = path.with_name(path.name + ".tmp")
